**Structure** (module `m2`, 16 min, 2 theory beats + 5 widgets):
`theory → plotImage → parametricExplorer → quiz → theory → code → sandbox` — starts on theory, no two theories adjacent, ends on a widget.
**Pedagogy (intuition-first, per the audience override):**
- **Beat 1** — "don't blur, filter adaptively"; despeckling as a two-axis trade-off (ENL vs edge/point preservation), bridged to the bilateral filter; inline **before/after** figure (raw 1-look | boxcar | Lee on the real tile).
- **PlotImage** — quantitative trade-off: boxcar buys higher ENL but collapses edge sharpness to ~13%, Lee holds ~42%. Full axes/units/legend/title; `sourceCode` reproduces the PNG byte-for-byte.
- **ParametricExplorer** — live boxcar-vs-Lee select + window slider on a synthetic 1-look scene (pure numpy/matplotlib, the Pyodide worker's only libs), with a cross-edge profile and ENL readout. Smoke-tested: ENL reads 1.0 raw → boxcar 173 → Lee 56.
- **Beat 2** — the Lee formula $\hat I = \bar I + W(I-\bar I)$, $W=1-C_u^2/C_i^2$ with **every symbol glossed** (meaning, unit, typical value); inline **CoV map** of the real tile showing the coastline glowing (Lee preserves) vs dark sea (Lee smooths); Frost / Refined Lee / NL-means as variants.
